win10xbox: kernelbase exports NlsGetCacheUpdateCount

The genuine gdi32full calls kernelbase!NlsGetCacheUpdateCount from GdiGetCharDimensions (any MessageBox sizing its text on the
native-GUI machine folders); Wine had it as a stub, so the first call raised EXCEPTION_WINE_STUB (0x80000100) and ended the
process (docs/slices/d3dsample.md round 3). The real function returns the NLS cache update counter that changes when the
locale changes; Wine reads its locale data once at load and never updates it, so the equivalent is a constant 0.

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/locale.c b/dlls/kernelbase/locale.c
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/locale.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/locale.c
@@ -763,6 +763,18 @@
 }
 
 
+/******************************************************************************
+ *	NlsGetCacheUpdateCount   (kernelbase.@)
+ *
+ * The real one returns the counter of NLS cache updates (locale changes); the genuine gdi32full compares it with the
+ * value it saw when it cached text metrics (GdiGetCharDimensions). Locale data is read once at load here and never
+ * updated, so the count never changes.
+ */
+ULONG WINAPI NlsGetCacheUpdateCount(void)
+{
+    return 0;
+}
+
 static int locale_return_data( const WCHAR *data, int datalen, LCTYPE type, WCHAR *buffer, int len )
 {
     if (type & LOCALE_RETURN_NUMBER)
diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/kernelbase.spec b/dlls/kernelbase/kernelbase.spec
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/kernelbase.spec
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/kernelbase.spec
@@ -1018,7 +1018,7 @@
 @ stub NlsDispatchAnsiEnumProc
 @ stub NlsEventDataDescCreate
 @ stub NlsGetACPFromLocale
-@ stub NlsGetCacheUpdateCount
+@ stdcall NlsGetCacheUpdateCount()
 @ stub NlsIsUserDefaultLocale
 @ stub NlsUpdateLocale
 @ stub NlsUpdateSystemLocale
